# Only a serial port that is no known GPS receiver is plugged in (a CH340 radar, 1a86:7523): Auto never opens it, the chip is
# the crossed-out dish; Settings > GPS receiver > Port lists it (and the hint row), and a port chosen there is opened
# (it sends nothing, so the dish stays crossed out). The synthetic feed "other" stands for that port.
title GPS: only another serial device, Auto leaves it alone
sizes 640x480 480x320 320x480
env DECKATLAS_DEMO 1
env DECKATLAS_GPS auto
env DECKATLAS_GPS_FEED other
env DECKATLAS_VIEW 48.889643,2.269995,16

wait 3000
shot no-receiver
expect text "Map"
key tab
key tab
wait 800
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
wait 400
shot settings-port-auto
expect text "Port"
key enter
wait 400
shot settings-port-chosen
expect text "ttyUSB0"
key tab
wait 3500
shot map-port-chosen
expect text "Map"
